## Summary

Implemented **`DET.NAV.FOCUS_ORDER`** as a deterministic keyboard focus-order check aligned with the source rule: tab order should follow visual reading order on sampled paths.

### Rule signals (from spec)

- **Pass:** Tab order matches top-to-bottom / left-to-right visual order.
- **Evidence:** Automated tab order (no AI).

### Implementation

**`design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-nav-focus-order.check.js`**

- Builds a browser tab sequence (positive `tabindex` first, then DOM order) for up to **48** visible tab stops.
- Flags:
  - **`positive-tabindex`** — any `tabindex > 0` (minor)
  - **`reverse-vertical`** — next stop jumps **>72px** upward (warn)
  - **`reverse-horizontal`** — same-row LTR move **>96px** left (warn; skipped when `dir=rtl`)
- Exports: `rule`, `run`, `collectNavFocusOrderReport`, `findingsFromNavFocusOrderReport`, `violationsFromFocusOrderSequence` (unit-testable).
- `run` uses `metrics.navFocusOrderReport` or live `page.evaluate()`.

**`design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`**

- Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **`implemented`**: `area: accessibility`, `scoreDimension: accessibilitySemanticsMeta`, `priorityWeight: 8`.

**`auditor-tests/det-nav-focus-order.test.js`**

- Covers violation detection, finding mapping, and `run()` with precomputed metrics.

**`design-rules/registry.generated.json`**

- Updated so `DET.NAV.FOCUS_ORDER` is **`implemented`** (coverage counts 35/15). Re-run blend to refresh **`fingerprint`** and **`generatedAt`**.

